{
  "_meta": {
    "table": "nutra_additives",
    "version": "0.1",
    "purpose": "D-139: the additives FSSAI's supplement rules point to. 5(4)(a) and its footnote: Appendix A's GMP table and Annexure 3 for every supplement (the 10 May 2022 order adds tablet excipients \"in addition to\" the GMP table, so it covers tablets too); 6(1)(e): tablets, capsules, pills and liquids use Annexure 3's list for tablets, capsules and syrups, other formats the 13.6 list. Found in a list: listed. Not found: \"we didn't find it in the lists\", never \"not permitted\" (names vary, and the Drugs and Cosmetics Rules' colour list isn't read).",
    "source": {
      "title": "FSS (Nutra) Regulations, 2022, Annexure 3, as operationalised by FSSAI's direction of 18 October 2022; FSSAI order of 10 May 2022",
      "url": "https://fssai.gov.in/docs/food-law/regulations/Direction_New_compressed.pdf",
      "read_on": "2026-09-30"
    },
    "rules": [
      "Names as printed, spelling included (\"Manitol\", \"Tocoferol\", \"Saff flower oil\"). Parsed from the text layer and checked against the page images, Annexure pp. 71 to 75.",
      "Upper-case names in the supplements list are groups (BENZOATES, PHOSPHATES...): matched by the group word on the pack's entry, as the list prints no INS for them.",
      "The list prints an en dash in \"Caramel III (en dash) Ammonia caramel\" and \"Caramel IV (en dash) Sulfite ammonia caramel\"; written here with a hyphen (no dashes in the project).",
      "`aliases` on a tablet row are spelling and salt variants used only to match a pack's wording to the row (\"Sodium benzoate\" to \"Benzoic acid and its salts\"); no sentence shows them.",
      "Tablet-list names mark an entry as an additive only for tablets, capsules and syrups: in a gummy or a powder, gelatin, sucrose or pectin are ingredients."
    ]
  },
